(vector (map (:adr/id 2790003333), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-3333 — Employment Agents and Contractors Placement Coordination"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3333)), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-3333), (:actor/name "Employment Placement Coordination Practice"), (:actor/domain :professional/employment-placement), (:actor/isco-08 "3333"), (:actor/wave 2), (:actor/robotics? true), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-candidate-record :propose-placement-match :flag-compliance-concern :coordinate-interview-schedule)), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-compliance-concern)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :candidate-verified :employer-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "finalize the hiring decision" "finalized the hiring decision" "finalize the rejection decision" "finalized the rejection decision" "finalize the candidate rejection" "finalized the candidate rejection" "approve the hiring decision" "approved the hiring decision" "deny the candidate application" "denied the candidate application" "reject the candidate application" "rejected the candidate application" "confirm the hiring decision" "confirmed the hiring decision" "execute the hiring decision" "executed the hiring decision" "issue the final hiring decision" "issued the final hiring decision" "finalize the candidate screening decision" "finalized the candidate screening decision" "screen out the candidate" "screened out the candidate" "採用決定を確定" "採用を確定した" "不採用決定を確定" "不採用を確定した" "候補者の応募を却下した" "候補者の応募を拒否した")), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-candidate-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-candidate-record :propose-placement-match :coordinate-interview-schedule}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-candidate-record :propose-placement-match :coordinate-interview-schedule :flag-compliance-concern}, :auto #{:log-candidate-record :propose-placement-match :coordinate-interview-schedule}}}"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3333"), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-3333"), (:test/counts "{:total 20, :assertions 51, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :candidate-verification :employer-verification :closed-op-allowlist)), (:test/simulator :placementops.actor-test), (:db/id -1), (:adr/body "# ADR 2790003333: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 3333 Employment Agents and Contractors placement-coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise — a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 3333 -- Employment Agents\nand Contractors** only.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id 3333 ...}` entry was\nverified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M -e\n\"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"3333\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling\npresent), and its `:name` read exactly \"Employment Agents and\nContractors\" -- confirming the premise. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3333` (`gh api` 404-\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit\npromote the `3333` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals), independently re-cloned and\nre-tested in this session (14 tests / 29 assertions green on a fresh\nclone before this actor's own code was written), adapted to employment\nplacement coordination.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3333` as an OSS placement-\ncoordination actor for employment agents and contractors, following the\nSAME governed-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Placement Advisor ⊣ PlacementOps Governor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- this is a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **placement coordination only**, never\nhiring/rejection/screening authority -- the domain-specific anti-\ndiscrimination guardrail for this vertical:\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-candidate-record` -- candidate profile/application intake\n  logging\n- `:propose-placement-match` -- candidate-to-employer matching\n  proposal (never finalizes hiring)\n- `:flag-compliance-concern` -- surface a discrimination/screening-bias\n  concern, ALWAYS escalates\n- `:coordinate-interview-schedule` -- interview scheduling proposal\n\nNo op in this allowlist can finalize a hiring decision, a candidate-\nrejection decision, or any placement decision that could constitute\ndiscriminatory screening -- such an op is structurally absent from the\nallowlist, not merely gated.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Candidate unverified** -- any proposal referencing a `:candidate-id`\n   must resolve to an independently `:registered?`/`:verified?`\n   candidate record. Never trusts the proposal's own claim.\n2. **Employer unverified** -- same, for any proposal referencing an\n   `:employer-id`.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist\n   is a HARD, PERMANENT block. This independently rejects any attempt\n   to slip in a `:finalize-hiring-decision`-shaped op.\n5. **Scope exclusion** -- independent of the op-allowlist check, any\n   proposal whose `:rationale` names a finalization/execution action\n   for a hiring, rejection or other placement decision (e.g. \"finalized\n   the hiring decision\", \"rejected the candidate application\") is a\n   HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally on content, not\n   just on the `:op` field.\n\n### Two ESCALATE (SOFT) gates plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-compliance-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless\n  of confidence or phase (independently agreed by both the governor's\n  `always-escalate-ops` and the phase table's `:auto` set, which never\n  contains this op at any phase 0-3, per this vertical's explicit\n  anti-discrimination guardrail: a flag-a-concern op must always\n  escalate and never be auto-commit-eligible).\n- a `:propose-placement-match` proposal at `:stake :high` -- a\n  high-stake candidate-to-employer match always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence.\n- (LLM confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for any\n  op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the\nsibling ISIC track)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"hiring\", \"rejection\", \"screening\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the happy path -- this is exactly the risk the domain\ndescription's own disclaimer language (\"never finalizes hiring\") could\ntrigger if phrased carelessly. This actor's\n`placementops.governor/scope-excluded-terms` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"approved the hiring decision\",\n\"rejected the candidate application\"), never bare nouns, and\n`placementops.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded` (or any other HARD violation). The mock advisor's own\ndefault rationale template (\"drafted <op> for candidate <id>[, employer\n<id>]\") was written to avoid any bare-noun collision by construction.\nGreen on first run in this session -- no self-trip was actually hit\nduring development, unlike some ISIC-track siblings that discovered and\nfixed the bug live; this ADR still documents the guard and its\nregression test since the risk class is real for this domain.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"3333\" ...}` entry is\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3333` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3333`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented count\n  bumped accordingly (recomputed from the live registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not by `grep -c`, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 20 tests, 51 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/counts`\n  and in the task report, independently re-verified against a fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- unlike the ISIC-track convention this batch's task brief\n  assumed, the reference `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` and other existing\n  `:implemented` ISCO actors (`cloud-itonami-isco-0110`,\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-1111`, live-checked via `gh api`) do NOT depend on\n  `kotoba-lang/technology` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation`\n  registry itself depends on it (to resolve `:required-technologies`\n  stacks), not individual actor repos. This ADR's actor mirrors the\n  live convention rather than the assumed one.\n- This session also found that `90-docs/adr` moved to an EDN-only SSoT\n  convention (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, landed the same day as this ADR)\n  -- new ADRs are a single-entity EDN vector with a `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`. This ADR follows the live\n  convention (EDN-only, matching the sibling `cloud-itonami-isic-*`\n  coverage ADRs already on `main`) rather than the paired-file\n  convention the task brief described.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Reusing ISIC 3313's `accountingsupport.governor` ceiling-based check\n  shape directly (e.g. a numeric fee ceiling per employer): rejected --\n  this vertical's defining risk is not an amount ceiling but a\n  categorical prohibition (never finalize a hiring/rejection/screening\n  decision), so the governor adds a closed op-allowlist HARD check and a\n  content-based scope-exclusion HARD check instead of (or in addition\n  to) a numeric ceiling, matching the domain-specific guardrail in the\n  task brief exactly.\n- Gating high-stake placement matches only via the op-level\n  `always-escalate-ops` set (as the reference does for `:approve-over-\n  ceiling-posting`): rejected in favor of a proposal-level `:stake`\n  check on `:propose-placement-match`, since stake varies per proposal\n  for this op (unlike the reference's ceiling check, which is itself an\n  entirely separate always-escalate op) -- a single op can be either\n  low-stake (auto-commit-eligible) or high-stake (always escalate)\n  depending on content, not identity.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"hiring\" \"rejection\"\n  \"screening\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  hiring/rejection/screening concepts to do its job (e.g. `:flag-\n  compliance-concern`'s purpose IS to discuss a screening-bias concern),\n  so a bare-noun list would have self-blocked the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals.")))
